WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.032
- Where is it?

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:06.427
- I put it over there.

00:00:06.427 --> 00:00:07.260
- By the couch?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.093
- Yeah.

00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:08.926
- Oh.

00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:15.119
An electric eel, magnificent.

00:00:24.673 --> 00:00:28.840
Our submarine is docked
here, in the Amazon River.

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:31.957
- We could have gone to the Orinoco River

00:00:31.957 --> 00:00:34.396
but our dear Desiree wouldn't fit.

00:00:34.396 --> 00:00:37.368
This is the only other place in the world

00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:39.341
to find electric eels.

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:41.012
- Exactement mon chéri.

00:00:41.012 --> 00:00:43.912
Electric eels are quite
the peculiar species.

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:46.319
They're like aquatic batteries.

00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:48.956
The majority of their
body is made up of organs

00:00:48.956 --> 00:00:51.054
that produce electricity.

00:00:51.054 --> 00:00:53.054
Listen, you can hear it.

00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:58.608
(electric static sound)

00:00:58.608 --> 00:01:00.093
They're also obligate air breathers,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.811
which means they must surface
every ten minutes or so

00:01:02.811 --> 00:01:04.435
to breathe above water.

00:01:04.435 --> 00:01:08.647
Scientists at Vanderbilt
University, you know, hold on.

00:01:08.647 --> 00:01:11.147
Let's get Kenneth on the line.

00:01:14.402 --> 00:01:17.466
Bonjour Kenneth, so I hear
your team has some interesting

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:18.549
findings, eh?

00:01:19.399 --> 00:01:21.102
- Yeah, we discovered
something really remarkable

00:01:21.102 --> 00:01:23.571
so when you threaten or
corner an electric eel

00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:27.066
it can leap out of the water
and put its chin onto you

00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:30.367
so that the current is sent
straight through your body

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.456
and back down to the water
giving maximal shock.

00:01:33.456 --> 00:01:34.789
- How, shocking.

00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:39.232
Now how do these eels
generate all that electricity?

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.488
- Well, they have modified
muscles that in the course

00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:44.461
of evolution are now just
used to generate electricity.

00:01:44.461 --> 00:01:47.755
And they line these up in
series to generate high voltages

00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:50.379
and create a very powerful shock.

00:01:50.379 --> 00:01:54.546
- Thanks Kenneth, and say hi
to the missus for me, okay.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.774
These eels might be
dangerous but once they shock

00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:04.796
their prey they need time to recharge.

00:02:04.796 --> 00:02:06.979
So, you probably won't get shocked.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:08.778
- Are we safe?

00:02:08.778 --> 00:02:10.414
There's no cover on the tank.

00:02:10.414 --> 00:02:11.497
- Yeah, sure.

